{"comments":"Viewport — A rendering target as a tensor computation space.\n\n## Design Philosophy\n\nA viewport is not a rectangle of pixels. It's a **tensor computation target**:\n\n```\nViewportTensor\n  { pixelShape: [1, 4, 1080, 1920]      -- What the display shows\n  , latentShape: [1, 4, 135, 240]       -- What we compute (8× downsample)\n  , physicalExtent: meters 0.53 × 0.30  -- Physical size (optional)\n  }\n```\n\n## Why This Matters\n\nAt billion-agent scale with diffusion rendering:\n- Same latent shape can render to any physical size\n- 20ft LED wall and smartwatch use same tensor computation\n- Resolution independence is built-in\n\n## The 20ft Screen Problem\n\n```\nScreen A: 1920×1080 on 24\" monitor (92 PPI)\nScreen B: 1920×1080 on 20ft LED wall (8 PPI)\n```\n\n**Same tensor shape. Same compute. Different physical interpretation.**\n\nThe tensor doesn't know or care about physical size. Physical size is\nmetadata for the display hardware, not the compute graph.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Hydrogen.Schema.Tensor.Shape (tensor shapes)\n- Hydrogen.Schema.Dimension.Device (pixel units, DPI)\n- Hydrogen.Schema.Temporal (frame rates)\n","declarations":[{"children":[{"comments":null,"info":{"arguments":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Prim"],"Record"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":["pixelShape",{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Tensor","Shape"],"Shape"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":["latentShape",{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Tensor","Shape"],"Shape"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":["physicalExtent",{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Data","Maybe"],"Maybe"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Spatial","Viewport"],"PhysicalExtent"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"}],"tag":"TypeApp"},{"annotation":[],"contents":["devicePixelRatio",{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Dimension","Device"],"DevicePixelRatio"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":["colorSpace",{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Spatial","Viewport"],"ColorSpace"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":["frameRate",{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Dimension","Temporal"],"FrameRate"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":["memoryLayout",{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Spatial","Viewport"],"MemoryLayout"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":["downsampleFactor",{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Prim"],"Int"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"tag":"REmpty"}],"tag":"RCons"}],"tag":"RCons"}],"tag":"RCons"}],"tag":"RCons"}],"tag":"RCons"}],"tag":"RCons"}],"tag":"RCons"}],"tag":"RCons"}],"tag":"TypeApp"}],"declType":"dataConstructor"},"sourceSpan":{"end":[282,4],"name":"../src/Hydrogen/Schema/Spatial/Viewport.purs","start":[254,24]},"title":"ViewportTensor"},{"comments":null,"info":{"declType":"instance","dependencies":[],"type":{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Data","Eq"],"Eq"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Spatial","Viewport"],"ViewportTensor"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"}],"tag":"TypeApp"}},"sourceSpan":{"end":[284,54],"name":"../src/Hydrogen/Schema/Spatial/Viewport.purs","start":[284,1]},"title":"eqViewportTensor"},{"comments":null,"info":{"declType":"instance","dependencies":[],"type":{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Data","Show"],"Show"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Spatial","Viewport"],"ViewportTensor"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"}],"tag":"TypeApp"}},"sourceSpan":{"end":[296,45],"name":"../src/Hydrogen/Schema/Spatial/Viewport.purs","start":[286,1]},"title":"showViewportTensor"}],"comments":"A viewport as a tensor computation target.\n\nThis is the fundamental abstraction for resolution-independent renderin